{"availability":"available","full":"david-andrew/sloppy-lang","name":"sloppy-lang","description":"A programming language developed by AI","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"C","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-08T10:00:17Z","updated":"2026-10-11T03:04:40Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://david-andrew.github.io/sloppy-lang/","topics":[],"demo":"https://sloppy-lang.org/playground/#example=rebound","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:48.366Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:48.366Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:48.366Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T06:14:48.366Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Sloppy is a small, compiled, statically typed language that feels like a scripting language, built for making games. sloppy game.jo compiles the whole program and runs it in a blink; sloppy build game.jo writes a standalone executable for Linux or Windows, and with target = wasm a single self-contained .html file that runs in a browser straight from disk.","A complete one: Rebound, an arcade game in one file. Turn a shield around the core to catch the turrets' bolts and send them back: blasts set off the turrets beside them, catches near the shield's edge bank off to other turrets, and every few turrets you choose an upgrade. Play it in the browser, or change it there in the playground.","In 3D: Breakwater, a first-person shooter in one file. Hold a platform at sea against waves of robots, with a shield that recharges, two weapons at a time, grenades and melee; animated glTF models, shadows and bloom. Play it in the browser."],"features":["Fast compiles. About 250,000 lines per second on one core (debug builds), roughly 20x","faster than gcc -O0. Hello world compiles and runs in 10 ms. There are no incremental builds and no build system: build options live in the source (build: block).","Edit while it runs. sloppy watch game.jo reloads the running game as you save: new code","takes over between two frames, and the game keeps its state, its window and what it loaded.","Fast programs. Release builds (opt = release) are within 1.5x of gcc -O2 on the"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/david-andrew/sloppy-lang/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"7e8afa04a5685b3ff39d3283ef3f86281dd97620780fb91f129f408fee49dd06","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:48.510Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:48.510Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Sloppy is a small, compiled, statically typed language that feels like a scripting language, built for making games. sloppy game.jo compiles the whole program and runs it in a blink; sloppy build game.jo writes a standalone executable for Linux or Windows, and with target = wasm a single self-contained .html file that runs in a browser straight from disk.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/david-andrew/sloppy-lang/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"Sloppy is a small, compiled, statically typed language that feels like a scripting language, built for making games. sloppy game.jo compiles the whole program and runs it in a blink; sloppy build game.jo writes a standalone executable for Linux or Windows, and with target = wasm a single self-contained .html file that runs in a browser straight from disk.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/david-andrew/sloppy-lang/blob/master/README.md"}],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"7e8afa04a5685b3ff39d3283ef3f86281dd97620780fb91f129f408fee49dd06","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/david-andrew/sloppy-lang/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:48.510Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-11T03:04:40Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/david-andrew/sloppy-lang/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:48.511Z","hash":"7e8afa04a5685b3ff39d3283ef3f86281dd97620780fb91f129f408fee49dd06","originalBytes":14797,"storedBytes":14797,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["